{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_density_boost_with_mr",
  "intent": "Boost cluster_density early-tour weight from 0.06 to 0.38, and add mean_remaining as a second cluster-core indicator with a bounded negative weight (-0.06*(1-p)). Include a small nonlinear cd^2 bonus (0.03*(1-p)) to disproportionately favor dense cluster cores over peripheral candidates. The (1-p) modulation confines all new influence to early tour, preserving the parent's late-tour return-aware closure. Targets cluster_loss (the parent's weakest family dimension); in uniform/grid, cd and mr vary less across candidates, so ranking shifts are benign.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "nonlinear"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f[\"distance\"]\n    r = f[\"return_distance\"]\n    nr = f[\"nearest_remaining\"]\n    mr = f[\"mean_remaining\"]\n    g = f[\"regret\"]\n    p = f[\"progress\"]\n    cd = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    return -d + (0.15 + 0.40 * p) * r + (0.35 - 0.20 * p) * g + (0.10 + 0.28 * (1 - p)) * cd - 0.08 * (1 - p) * nr - 0.06 * (1 - p) * mr + 0.03 * (1 - p) * cd * cd\n",
  "source": "live_llm",
